# The build context is what the Dockerfile COPYs: requirements.txt, app/,
# library/, logs/, docs/, and the claim-evidence paths (tests/, .github/,
# deploy/, Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml). Excluding one of those breaks the
# build at "failed to compute cache key ... not found", which is what happened
# while docs/ was listed here and the Azure tab needed it inside the image.
# Keeping .git and the local virtualenv out of it makes the image build faster
# and stops a developer's .venv (with its host-specific binaries) reaching the
# 512MB deployment by accident.
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
artifacts
render.yaml
.DS_Store
# tests/, .github/, deploy/, tools/, Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml are
# deliberately NOT ignored: market claims cite them as evidence and the image
# ships them (see the "claim evidence" block in the Dockerfile). Excluding one
# of them breaks the build at "failed to compute cache key ... not found".
# tools/ui is the Tailwind build for the dashboard's static assets; nothing at
# runtime reads it and no claim cites it.
tools/ui
